WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.590
How do nonprofits and coalitions ask
better questions before changing a

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:07.310
program? Start with the decision.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.130
A needs assessment asks who needs
support and where access breaks down.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:18.210
A program evaluation asks how an
existing service is working

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:21.070
and what the team should test next.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.050
Think of a referral as a relay.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:28.250
A partner may think the handoff is
complete when it sends the contact

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:32.570
details. The person waiting for a call
may see it differently.

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:38.410
Ask participants, staff, and partner
organizations about the same steps,

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.530
from referral to first contact and
follow-up.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.510
Imagine a coalition whose food support
referrals keep stalling.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:51.550
Interview people who reached intake and
people who stopped.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:54.710
Check when callbacks actually happened.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.410
If missed callbacks emerge as a barrier,
test scheduled callbacks with one

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.230
partner and see what changes.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:07.550
Use the worksheet to name the decision,
pick the evidence, and assign

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:08.950
someone to review it.

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:13.910
If your organization needs help planning
interviews or a qualitative study,

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.450
talk with us at PRC Impact.

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.890
Find the guide and start a project at
prcimpact.com.
